# TODO_hacks
#
# Known consolidation debt and implicit dependencies that should be
# made structural. Items here are "works but fragile" — they won't
# break today but will bite when something gets renamed/moved.

## DAG builder functions referenced as strings

The codegen registry stores graph builder names as strings:

    ToolDef::new(..., "build_makegen_graph", "")

Then testgen.rs hardcodes the actual function calls separately. Renaming
a builder function won't trigger a compile error — it silently breaks at
runtime. Should use function pointers or a trait-based dispatch instead.

Files:
  - core/codegen/src/registry.rs  (graph_builder field on ToolDef)
  - gunbc-dag/src/bin/testgen.rs  (hardcoded calls to builder functions)

## "buck-out/gen" hardcoded in 4+ locations

The output directory appears as a literal string in multiple files. If the
output dir ever changes, these won't update together. Should be a single
constant in gunbc-ir or similar.

Files:
  - core/codegen/src/main.rs       ("buck-out/gen/bin", "buck-out/gen/lib")
  - gunbc-dag/src/makegen/render.rs ("buck-out/gen/.codegen-stamp")
  - gunbc-dag/src/ci/ops.rs        ("buck-out/gen/bin" existence check)
  - core/codegen/src/registry.rs   ("buck-out/" in core_outputs())

## Codegen source tracking directories are static

The Makefile's CODEGEN_SOURCES variable tracks core/codegen/src and
core/ir/src, but this list is hardcoded in render.rs. If codegen gains
a new source dependency (e.g. a new core/lang/src crate), the stamp
won't track it and stale artifacts won't trigger rebuilds.

Files:
  - gunbc-dag/src/makegen/render.rs (line ~156, hardcoded find paths)

## Meta-target dependency strings not verified

Meta-targets reference other targets by name ("testgen-check", "fmt-fix",
"lint-fix") as hardcoded strings. Renaming or removing a target won't
cause a compile error — just a broken Makefile at runtime.

Files:
  - gunbc-dag/src/makegen/registry.rs (default_meta_targets(), fix_deps)
